  "lineage_conclusion": {
    "abi": "The source-065 host checker shared.h and source-067 shared.h match byte-for-byte. This is a necessary ABI check for the prepared host invocation, not proof that the checker was compiled against source-067 or that the selector-5 production world ran.",
    "cause": "The source-063 and source-067 top-level matter_kernels.metal translation units have the same SHA, but quoted include resolution is relative to the translation unit directory. In the frozen source-063 build this resolves its frozen fgmres.metalinc (which has no graph kernels), not the graph overlay include offered through -I. The source-067 translation unit resolves source-067 fgmres.metalinc, which includes the graph kernels. The five kernel function bodies in source-067 and the old overlay are byte-identical by extracted body hash; build lineage nevertheless differs.",
    "run209": "The loaded source-063 metallib lacks all five graph kernel export names. Host reported first missing production function nm_fgmres_graph_factor_patches and exited before native output was written.",
    "run210": "The fresh source-067 metallib has all five graph names and dispatch completed all five kernels on Apple M4 with status 0. Arithmetic checking remains separate and reports one per-patch residual over the existing 1e-3 gate."
  },
